cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Starlapse sky dataset: sky brightness and meteors measured from iPhone stacks"
abstract: >-
  Night-sky readings contributed by people photographing the sky with Starlapse, an iPhone
  long-exposure camera, who opted in. Each reading gives sky surface brightness in
  V mag/arcsec², Bortle class and naked-eye limiting magnitude, measured from the catalogue
  stars (Yale Bright Star Catalogue) in the stack itself, together with the per-star
  photometry it was computed from, so it can be recomputed with a better calibration.
  Detector sessions add meteors placed on the sky with their associated shower.
  Locations rounded to 0.1°. Photos are published alongside on Hugging Face.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Salavatov"
    given-names: "Rustam"
    alias: "fortunto2"
  - name: "Starlapse contributors"
keywords:
  - light pollution
  - sky quality meter
  - night sky brightness
  - meteors
  - citizen science
  - smartphone photometry
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fortunto2/starlapse"
url: "https://starlapse.app"
